From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicola Ferralis <ferralis@generalflash.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 17:25:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ext: mixed goals with XY-datum cavities, stacks picked by
 "at" and top features written with nz=+1

Training mixed goals (and the new suites mixed_at / mixed_at_long) gain two groups, after the
others as in a pump casing: a closed cavity on an XY datum plane, and a stack (neck, flange,
bore, mirrored bolt holes) on the top face or a side face whose faces are picked with "at".
Half of them write top-face features with an explicit normal nz=+1 and z. Before, nz=+1 only
came with "off" (datum planes), so a model sketched the S 80 casing's top flange on Plane:XY.
The mixed / mixed_long suites and every other split keep their goals.
