 Patch 0011: mixed goals may also carry one group on the bottom face (Face-Z).
 
+Patch 0016 (training goals and the suites mixed_at / mixed_at_long only; the mixed and
+mixed_long suites are unchanged): two more groups, after the others as in a pump casing,
+  - a closed cavity on an XY datum plane (nz=+1 with "off"), single or a row;
+  - a stack on the top face or a side face, every feature's face picked with "at": a neck,
+    optionally a wider flange on it, then a bore and / or bolt holes in the flange rim
+    (mirrored), or a hole in the neck's end;
+and half the goals write their top-face features the way a planner may: with an explicit
+normal nz=+1 and z (sometimes also "at"). Before this patch nz=+1 only ever came with "off",
+so a model read any nz=+1 as a datum plane (the S 80 casing built its top flange on
+Plane:XY instead of Face+Z).
+
 Neither family produces a composition upstream holds out (goals.heldout_composition): no
 boss_box at all, no mirrored hole_std, no patterned pocket_rect.
 
